{
  "name": "What Do I Need to Know Before Installing Ceramic Tile?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about new ceramic tile? Great choice! Here’s a quick checklist to get you ready. First, assess your subfloor: Is it solid and even? If not, it needs cleaning and leveling, and possibly some structural shoring up if it's carrying a lot of weight. Next, consider what kind of underlayment might be needed—do you need crack isolation, waterproofing, or vapor control? These aren't always obvious but are super important for longevity. Third, have you picked out your specific tile and discussed the right mortar and grout with your installer? Different tiles and environments need different adhesives and grout types. Fourth, be aware of the timeline. Most mortar systems need about 24 hours to cure before you can even walk on the tile or grout it, so plan for some downtime. Finally, make sure your installer has experience with your chosen materials and offers a good warranty. A professional like us can guide you through these questions, ensuring a smooth process and a beautiful, durable result. Ready to get started? Give HH Remodeling LLC a call!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
